Attach a command verb to an object, or clear one.

usage: @setverb <object> <word> <prog-id> [argspec]
       @setverb <object> <word> -

A command verb binds a word a player can type to a program. It is stored as
the property verb.<word> on an object; when a player in scope types that
word, the dispatcher runs the program against the object the verb was found
on. Scope is searched in order: the actor, the actor's location, the
actor's held items, then the room contents.

  <object>    the cache id of the object to carry the verb, e.g. rooms/cave.
  <word>      the command word (letters, digits, dash, underscore).
  <prog-id>   a bound program, named without the programs/ prefix, e.g. a
              program built with @compile. It must already exist.
  [argspec]   an optional pattern for the rest of the command (see below).

The second form, with a single '-' in place of the program, clears the
object's own verb.<word>.

Argument spec tokens:
  <obj>           an object name in scope
  <player>        a player name
  <atom>          any single word
  <atom=word>     a specific word; <atom=a|b|c> any of several
  <any>           all remaining text
  a bare word     shorthand for <atom=word>

Wizard only. This sets the object's own verb; a verb inherited from a
prototype is not changed.

Examples:
  @setverb rooms/cave examine look-kp <obj>
      Typing "examine ember" in the cave runs program look-kp on the
      named object.
  @setverb rooms/cave examine -
      Remove that verb.

See also @compile, @chown, help addverb, help programs, help kobold.
